WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.600
The world's biggest democracy just had
an election.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.760
The world’s biggest democratic election

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.980
It’s a marathon election

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.180
A mammoth undertaking

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.400
It’s the world’s biggest exercise in democracy

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.400
In India, voters picked its central government for the next five years.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.660
An eighth of the world's population was eligible to vote in this election.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:29.840
This year, 2019, there are
900 million eligible voters in India

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.100
making this the largest Democratic exercise in the history of humanity.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.040
But this isn't a
video about Indian politics,

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.240
because before India's people can even cast their vote, the election needs to come to them

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.800
Polling stations need to be set up
wherever people live.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.340
And in one of the largest and most populous countries in the world,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.520
that isn't an easy task.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.460
India has to reach voters in coastal cities in
the south, in the rural regions of the west,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.180
and jungles to the east and
everywhere in between.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.840
And what's more, they want every Indian
citizen to be within 2 km of a voting station.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:12.180
That's only about 25 city blocks no matter where you are in the country.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.760
It's an incredibly ambitious
goal and yet, somehow they're able to do it.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:22.560
This is the biggest election in the
world and I wanted to know how does it work.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.760
Every election a team of government
officials and security forces,

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.100
get on a boat in the east of India to take off
towards this island.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.800
They travel about 100 km to get here, all to
securely deliver these

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:05.000
Electronic Voting Machines or EVMS, the instrument that
logs India's votes,

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.700
the heart of this elaborate election process.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:15.480
India has 2.3 million voting machines
for its 900 million voters.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.800
So getting these machines close to every voter is a big logistical undertaking.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.520
That's why India doesn't have a single Election Day,

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.860
instead, it's closer to an election month

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:28.700
with multiple phases that last weeks.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.660
This process takes more than 
11 million election officials and security forces,

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:36.860
who move from polling station to polling station to polling station

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.720
from densely populated cities to the rural areas where the majority of Indians live.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:51.440
Once on the island with the EVMs, officials pile on to bike carts and head towards the polling station.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.420
Once they arrive, they begin setting
everything up for the vote .

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:37.320
On Election Day, voters line up, cast their vote, and get
their fingers inked to prevent double voting.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.260
This is where the process ends
for the voters,

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.500
but for the election officials this is just the beginning.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:54.920
Driving a boat out to a remote island is just one of many ways that officials reach every voter.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:00.380
India's vast and diverse terrain requires transportation methods of all kinds,

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.780
like in the jungles
of this northern state where elephants

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:08.980
transport voting machines to reach a
remote town or in the Himalayas where

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.840
officials hike for hours to bring EVMS
for election day.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.860
Helicopters, trains, they even use camels.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:20.840
But what makes India's elections so impressive isn't just how they reach everyone in such a big country,

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.780
that's just half the battle.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:27.780
It's also the ways they try to include voters of all backgrounds into the process,

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.760
a challenge that has been a part of India's elections since the very beginning.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.080
India has 22 official languages and hundreds of dialects

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:41.500
and when India became an independent nation, less than a quarter of the population could read and write.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:47.060
The newly formed Election Commission of India created a range of symbols to correspond

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:51.780
to each political party, like an elephant, a lotus, a hand or even an alarm clock

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:58.160
so that from the beginning all people regardless of literacy level and language could vote with confidence.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.720
Since 1947,  the literacy
rate has increased significantly,

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:09.180
but it's still only 75 percent, so these
symbols are still useful to many when casting a vote.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.120
But this is a massive sprawling operation

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:16.300
and over the years it's run
into some pretty serious problems

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:21.100
like allegations of election rigging and
problems with a practice called booth capture,

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.240
where gangs actually take over
polling stations and tamper with the elections.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:30.960
It's partly because of these problems that the Commission introduced these voting machines in the 1990s.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.860
It also increased security around the elections.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:41.900
These efforts to include all voters and protect elections seem to be working.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:46.020
In 2019, India saw the highest
voter turnout yet

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:49.940
and for the first time women voted just as much as men.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:01.400
India's elections are only getting bigger and more complicated.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:04.440
India has one of the fastest growing populations in the world.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:09.640
and in 2020, young people will make up
more than a third of the country.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:25.540
This is the biggest election in the
world that takes millions of officials

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:29.520
fanning out across a massive country to
help hundreds of millions vote.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:34.000
Every part of this, the symbols, the elephants, the
boats, the machines

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:39.160
shows how hard it is to make sure that everyone in a country this large can participate

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:43.340
and all without going more than two kilometers
from home.

